!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/a-reference-to-a-constructor-in-an-ordinary-schema-expected.tn"
!!schema:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §4.1, [TSON-SCHEMA] §4.2"
  description: """
    Core's `ref` refuses a constructor as the kernel's does: `T` is a type of the writer's own namespace, and
    an ordinary schema's namespace holds no constructor, so `ref<record>` names nothing a value can be of. The
    names of the types built with `record` are `kind<record>`. Refused where it is written.
    """
  meta: "meta.tn"
  import: ["core.tn"]
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
